  "_link_comment": "Inter-node: 16 Gbps / 0.3 ms measured on the 10.212 fabric. Intra-node: same-host P/D handoff, measured ~0-2 ms for a 512-token prefix, modelled as 50 GB/s over PCIe with 1 us per-layer latency. Declaring the intra-node link switches the topology to [tp, slots_per_node, num_nodes] so the network model can tell a same-domain handoff from a cross-domain one.",
  "_handoff_comment": "kv_egress_gbps caps the P/D handoff path at min(wire, declared). Wire = 2 GB/s (measured intranet). Producer ceiling measured on the native NixlConnector is 115-314 MB/s (184 MB per 1250-token handoff in 585-731 ms) -- but it does NOT bind at this trace's 254-token prompts, where a handoff measures 40-90 ms (37 MB, i.e. 0.4-0.9 GB/s): the engine bursts small transfers. So this short-prompt config keeps the wire value (2.0) and reproduces the deployment's sustained 14 req/s. For KV-heavy traces use kv_egress_gbps = 0.26 (see the long-prompt variant), where the producer does bind. Known residual: ASTRA-Sim's congestion-unaware backend charges every per-layer send on the instance's own timeline without overlapping it with compute, so with the 0.26 cap a single 254-token handoff costs 425 ms in simulation against ~90 ms measured -- an overlapped transfer model is the open follow-up.",
